A window's declared title reached no platform at all.

And a child was added through a switch over C types -- two of them, actually:
gtk4's cgo path knew seven parents and its wrapped path three, so a frame or a
popover in wrapped mode fell through to raw cgo in a file built without cgo.
The title is now `cgo.SnglToplevelSetTitle`, and a child goes through the
runtime's `sngl_box_append` (`cgo.SnglBoxAppend`), which asks the parent what
it is. The vbox nests so the append is a real parent-child one; the window's
own child goes to it through `cgo.SnglToplevelAppend` instead.
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        gtk4
    }
}

window(title="Counter") {
    var count int = 0

    vbox {
        text(value=string(count))
        button(text="+", @click { count = count + 1 })
    }
}
